<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Nudge Track tool palette (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual + behavioural PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms
    `Forms/Guidance/FormNudge` (FormNudge.cs + FormNudge.designer.cs), per AAP §0.3.3 —
    never a redesign (no new colours, no relayout, no UX change). FormNudge is a small,
    borderless, fixed-size floating tool palette that nudges the active guidance track:
    zero the offset, snap to the pivot, nudge left/right by the snap distance, nudge by
    half the tool width, and set the snap distance via the on-screen keypad. It floats over
    the main FormGPS window and persists its own location in Settings.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind (FormNudgeView.axaml.cs, partial class
    AgOpenGPS.Views.FormNudgeView : Window) owns ALL behaviour, NOT this markup:
      * This view is IMPERATIVE / code-behind-driven, not MVVM: there is intentionally NO
        x:DataType, NO DataContext and NO {Binding}. The x:Name'd controls below are the
        entire integration surface and keep their ORIGINAL WinForms names so the migrated
        code-behind addresses them exactly as FormNudge.cs did.
      * NO Click= attributes are declared here on purpose — the code-behind subscribes each
        handler by name (reproducing the WinForms handlers), so the view compiles
        independently of whatever handler names the code-behind chooses:
          - btnZeroMove     -> trk.NudgeDistanceReset() + UpdateMoveLabel()
          - btnSnapToPivot  -> trk.SnapToPivot()        + UpdateMoveLabel()
          - btnAdjLeft      -> trk.NudgeTrack(-snapAdj)  + UpdateMoveLabel()
          - btnAdjRight     -> trk.NudgeTrack(+snapAdj)  + UpdateMoveLabel()
          - btnHalfToolLeft -> trk.NudgeTrack(-(tool.width - tool.overlap) * 0.5)
          - btnHalfToolRight-> trk.NudgeTrack(+(tool.width - tool.overlap) * 0.5)
          - nudSnapDistance -> opens the numeric keypad (FormNumeric) and stores
                               ToolSettings.setAS_snapDistance (NudlessNumericUpDown.ShowKeypad
                               is REPLACED by FormNumeric per the sibling contract).
          - bthOK           -> Close() (the WinForms DialogResult.Yes handler merely closed).
        lblOffset is refreshed by the code-behind (UpdateMoveLabel / the 3 s timer tick);
        the literals below are design-time placeholders overwritten at runtime.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormNudge.designer.cs exactly (lines 258-274) and folds in the
    FormNudge.cs Win32 overrides (lines 143-207):
      ClientSize 180 x 410              ->  Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window)
      Min/MaximumSize both 180 x 410    ->  MinWidth=MaxWidth=180, MinHeight=MaxHeight=410 + CanResize="False"
      BackColor LightSteelBlue          ->  Background="LightSteelBlue"
      FormBorderStyle.None              ->  SystemDecorations="None". This subsumes the Win32
            CreateParams CS_DROPSHADOW drop-shadow and the WndProc caption-drag/maximise-block
            hack; the borderless drag is reimplemented in code-behind via BeginMoveDrag, and a
            drop shadow is cosmetic/best-effort (omitted). TransparencyLevelHint left at default.
      ShowInTaskbar = false             ->  ShowInTaskbar="False"
      StartPosition (restored in Load)  ->  WindowStartupLocation="Manual" (code-behind restores
            setWindow_formNudgeLocation in Opened, clamping on-screen as FormNudge.cs did).
      this.Text = ""                    ->  Title=""
      (not TopMost in source)           ->  Topmost="False" (parity — floating but not topmost)
      Font Tahoma                       ->  FontFamily="Tahoma"; children carry point sizes
            converted to Avalonia DIP as (pt * 96 / 72): 14.25pt -> 19, 18pt -> 24.

    IMAGES: the seven glyphs are served from the GPS assembly ("AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs.
    NOTE (resource-path provenance): the agent prompt text said avares://AgOpenGPS/Resources/…,
    but the assets physically live in SourceCode/GPS/btnImages/ and every sibling GPS Avalonia
    view (143 references) consumes them from btnImages/ — the prompt's own "consistent with
    sibling views" qualifier resolves to btnImages/. Using btnImages/ here is what makes the
    glyphs actually render, i.e. what delivers the required 1:1 visual parity.

    No WinForms, no OpenTK, no GMap, no ColorPicker types are referenced. Avalonia 11.3.x.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormNudgeView"
        Title=""
        Width="180"
        Height="410"
        MinWidth="180"
        MaxWidth="180"
        MinHeight="410"
        MaxHeight="410"
        CanResize="False"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        Topmost="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="Manual"
        Background="LightSteelBlue"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <!--
        Styles reproduce the WinForms button appearances:

        Button.flatImage — the seven image glyph buttons were FlatStyle.Flat with
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 and BackColor = Transparent (FormNudge.designer.cs). The
        template overrides force the Fluent Button's PART_ContentPresenter to stay transparent in
        the default, :pointerover and :pressed states so no hover/press fill boxes the glyph —
        the same technique used by the sibling FormPanView / FormColorSectionView.

        Button.numeric — nudSnapDistance was a NudlessNumericUpDown (ReadOnly, value display +
        keypad-on-click). Reproduced as a bordered, centred value box (AliceBlue fill, 1 px
        border), mirroring the sibling FormSteerView numeric-entry buttons.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="Button.numeric">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="AliceBlue" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root Canvas reproduces the WinForms absolute Location/Size layout for pixel-accurate
        1:1 parity on this fixed-size palette (the same Canvas approach used by the sibling
        FormPanView / FormShiftPosView). Every Canvas.Left/Top/Width/Height below is the exact
        designer value.
    -->
    <Canvas Width="180" Height="410">

        <!-- lblOffset: live nudge-offset readout. Designer (4,10), AutoSize, Tahoma 14.25pt Bold
             -> 19 DIP, black on transparent, centred. Text is a design-time placeholder; the
             code-behind overwrites it (UpdateMoveLabel / timer tick). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblOffset"
                   Canvas.Left="4" Canvas.Top="10"
                   FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="Black"
                   Background="Transparent"
                   TextAlignment="Center"
                   Text="0.35 &gt;" />

        <!-- WhiteSmoke panel: stands in for the WinForms tableLayoutPanel1 (BackColor WhiteSmoke).
             Designer (7,38) 166 x 302. The inner Canvas hosts the seven controls at their
             within-panel Location coordinates (relative to the panel origin). -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="7" Canvas.Top="38"
                Width="166" Height="302"
                Background="WhiteSmoke">
            <Canvas>

                <!-- btnZeroMove: zero the nudge offset. Designer (7,10) 69x58, glyph SteerZero. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnZeroMove"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Canvas.Left="7" Canvas.Top="10"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Zero nudge offset">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SteerZero.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnSnapToPivot: snap the track to the vehicle pivot. Designer (90,10) 69x58, glyph SnapToPivot. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnSnapToPivot"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Canvas.Left="90" Canvas.Top="10"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Snap to pivot">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapToPivot.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnAdjLeft: nudge the track left by the snap distance. Designer (7,90) 69x58, glyph SnapLeft. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnAdjLeft"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Canvas.Left="7" Canvas.Top="90"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge track left">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapLeft.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnAdjRight: nudge the track right by the snap distance. Designer (90,90) 69x58, glyph SnapRight. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnAdjRight"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Canvas.Left="90" Canvas.Top="90"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge track right">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapRight.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- nudSnapDistance: snap-distance value box (was NudlessNumericUpDown, ReadOnly,
                     Max 1000, Value 800, Tahoma 18pt Bold -> 24 DIP, centred). Designer (51,166)
                     64x36. Content "8" is a design-time placeholder overwritten at runtime; the
                     code-behind opens FormNumeric on click and saves setAS_snapDistance. -->
                <Button x:Name="nudSnapDistance"
                        Classes="numeric"
                        Canvas.Left="51" Canvas.Top="166"
                        Width="64" Height="36"
                        FontSize="24" FontWeight="Bold"
                        Content="8"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Snap distance" />

                <!-- btnHalfToolLeft: nudge left by half the tool width. Designer (7,227) 69x58, glyph SnapLeftHalf. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnHalfToolLeft"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Canvas.Left="7" Canvas.Top="227"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge half tool width left">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapLeftHalf.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnHalfToolRight: nudge right by half the tool width. Designer (90,227) 69x58, glyph SnapRightHalf. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnHalfToolRight"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Canvas.Left="90" Canvas.Top="227"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge half tool width right">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapRightHalf.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

            </Canvas>
        </Border>

        <!-- bthOK: close the palette. Designer (58,346) 64x56, OK64 glyph (was BackgroundImage,
             ImageLayout.Zoom -> Image Stretch="Uniform"). Flat/transparent like the rest. -->
        <Button x:Name="bthOK"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="58" Canvas.Top="346"
                Width="64" Height="56"
                AutomationProperties.Name="OK">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
